"status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-13","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-21","committee":"Strategy and Change Scrutiny Panel","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-22","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-23","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Pension Fund Panel","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Business rates collection 2.42% behind target, and declining 2.41% year-on-year","lead":"Year-on-year business rates collection decline, beyond government billing delays, signals underlying income risk affecting cash flow and medium-term revenue.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a351.3m of capital schemes decommissioned including 57 Greenford Rd housing block (\u00a332.8m) cancelled","lead":"Capital cancellations of this scale reduce investment capacity; loss of \u00a332.8m housing investment matters given the paper's identification of temporary accommodation cost pressures.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"DSG deficit forecast to grow to \u00a334.6m by year-end, driven by rising EHCP placement demand","lead":"DSG deficit is a balance sheet liability even if ring-fenced; structural EHCP demand growth represents ongoing recurring pressure that affects financial ratios.","iso":"2026-09-09","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","headline":"Business rates collection 2.42% behind target, and declining 2.41% year-on-year","detail":"Business rates collection in Q1 is 2.42% behind the 27.70% target (\u00a34.994m shortfall). The council attributes this partly to 'delays on the billing process due to government legislation changes' which should recover later in the year. However, collection is also 2.41% below the same period last year, suggesting underlying collection risk beyond timing.","category":"income","matters":"Year-on-year business rates collection decline, beyond government billing delays, signals underlying income risk affecting cash flow and medium-term revenue.","figures":"\u00a34.994m behind target (2.42%); 25.28% actual vs 27.70% target; down 2.41% year-on-year","quote":"Business rates collection is 2.42% behind target which equates to \u00a34.994m. The figure of 25.28% is 2.41% below the previous year.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","headline":"\u00a351.3m of capital schemes decommissioned including 57 Greenford Rd housing block (\u00a332.8m) cancelled","detail":"The council is removing \u00a351.287m from the capital programme. The 57 Greenford Rd housing block purchase (\u00a332.833m) is cancelled because 'the developer has withdrawn the offer to the council'. Stanhope Primary School development (\u00a317.942m) is also decommissioned as the land sale capital receipt did not materialise. These cancellations substantially reduce housing investment delivery.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital cancellations of this scale reduce investment capacity; loss of \u00a332.8m housing investment matters given the paper's identification of temporary accommodation cost pressures.","figures":"\u00a351.287m total decommissioned; \u00a332.833m (57 Greenford Rd housing); \u00a317.942m (Stanhope Primary)","quote":"the purchase of the 57 Greenford Rd housing block that will no longer go ahead as the developer has withdrawn the offer to the council (\u00a332.833m)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","headline":"DSG deficit forecast to grow to \u00a334.6m by year-end, driven by rising EHCP placement demand","detail":"The opening DSG deficit was \u00a318.121m. In-year movements of \u00a316.498m will push the closing balance to \u00a334.619m. This is driven by increasing demand for Education, Health and Care Plan (EHCP) payments across mainstream, academy and independent schools. While government has signalled a High Needs Stability Grant covering 90% of the historic deficit, the ongoing annual deterioration continues.","category":"demand","matters":"DSG deficit is a balance sheet liability even if ring-fenced; structural EHCP demand growth represents ongoing recurring pressure that affects financial ratios.","figures":"Opening balance \u00a318.121m; annual deterioration \u00a316.498m; projected closing \u00a334.619m","quote":"the forecast is estimating a deficit on DSG of \u00a316.498m, which is due to an increase in the High Needs Block across several areas relating to Education Health and Care Plan (EHCP) payments to schools","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","headline":"Only 30% of \u00a311.9m approved savings achieved by Q1; \u00a32.6m at risk of not delivering","detail":"The council approved \u00a311.937m of net savings for 2026/27. At Q1, only \u00a33.604m (30.19%) have been achieved, with \u00a32.595m (21.74%) flagged as at risk. Children's Services is particularly weak at 22.82% achievement with \u00a31.495m red-rated.","category":"savings","matters":"Weak savings delivery early in the year signals the council will need alternative budget actions, indicating execution and financial resilience risk.","figures":"\u00a33.604m achieved (30.19%); \u00a32.595m at risk (21.74%); \u00a35.738m in progress","quote":"At the end of Q1, \u00a33.604m (30.19%) of the savings have been achieved with \u00a32.595m (21.74%) identified at being risk","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-09","committee":"Cabinet","paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","headline":"Adult social care placement costs driving two-thirds of service overspend, a structural demand pressure","detail":"Adult Services & Public Health is forecasting \u00a312.459m overspend, of which \u00a312.849m is attributed to long-term placements for learning disability, mental health and older adults. The paper identifies 'high-cost clients' as a key risk, indicating this pressure is expected to persist.","category":"demand","matters":"Demand-led social care pressures that exceed budgets represent recurring, uncontrollable costs that affect financial sustainability and credit risk.","figures":"\u00a312.459m Adult Services overspend; \u00a312.849m from long-term placements","quote":"\u00a312.849m pressure relating to the cost of long-term learning disability, mental health & older adults placements.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-09"},"name":"Ealing","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":false,"headline":"Business rates collection 2.42% behind target, and declining 2.41% year-on-year","lead":"Year-on-year business rates collection decline, beyond government billing delays, signals underlying income risk affecting cash flow and medium-term revenue.","also":["12 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Health and Adult Social Services Scrutiny Panel on 2026-09-17","n_findings":13,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Budget Monitoring Report Quarter 1 202627 FINAL","top_paper_url":"https://ealing.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s26905/26905.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":70,"news_drafts_total":3}}